### 2.5 Infrastructure Traceability: From Claim to Code

Every reproducibility claim in this thesis is traceable through the infrastructure stack:

| Claim | Infrastructure | Evidence Location | External Reproducibility |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Deterministic randomness** | Fixed seed, JAX PRNG | `conftest.py` line 115, controlled by `rng_key = jr.PRNGKey(42)` | Identical seed 42 → identical sequence |
| **Environment reproducibility** | Dependency pinning | `pyproject.toml` lines 7–26, enforces jax>=0.4.0, numpy>=2.0.0 | `pip install malthusjax[cuda13]` recovers environment |
| **Test command consistency** | Makefile canonicalization | `Makefile` lines 30–40, makes test always runs with coverage | `git show v1.0:Makefile \| grep "^test:"` recovers exact command |
| **Benchmark standardization** | Benchmark group targets | `Makefile` lines 60–80, test-bench-group-05 always runs same tests | `make test-bench-group-05` on external machine runs identical benchmark |
| **Multi-seed isolation** | BenchmarkRunner + fixtures | `conftest_benchmarks.py` lines 475+, each seed independent lifecycle | 100 seeds run in parallel, one timeout ≠ total failure |
| **Canonical initialization** | Shared population factory | `conftest_benchmarks.py` lines 212–230, both frameworks call same function | MalthusJAX and Evosax start from identical genes |
| **JIT compilation isolation** | Warmup + block_until_ready | `conftest_benchmarks.py` line 414 (_setup), compilation before timing | Timing excludes XLA overhead, reflects algorithm only |
| **Bulk GPU transfer** | Centralized device_get | `conftest_benchmarks.py` line 430, single jax.device_get() call | No PCIe latency artifacts in per-generation measurements |
| **Version control snapshot** | Git infrastructure versioning | `git tag v1.0-thesis-experiments`, commit includes all infra | Reviewers 5 years later do `git show v1.0:conftest.py` |

**Implication**: Every result in this thesis is *traceable back to specific code*. Readers skeptical of any claim can examine the relevant file and line number. This is the definition of **audit-able research**.

