### 2.4 Ellipsoidal Function (Dimension 10)
**Location**: `results/thesis/convergence_ellipsoidal_dim10/`

#### Summary Table
| Pipeline | Best Fitness (Mean ± StdDev) | Median | Selection Impact |
|----------|---|---|---|
| malthusjax_roulette | -408.60 ± 53.12 | -403.70 | **BEST MalthusJAX** — diversity advantage |
| malthusjax_tournament | -2229.04 ± 1542.87 | -2016.01 | Trapped in ravines |
| malthusjax_default | -2440.03 ± 1802.16 | -1920.75 | Elite pool fails on ill-conditioned |
| evosax_differential_evolution | -193.86 ± 0.00 | -193.86 | Problem-agnostic (invariant) |
| evosax_simplega | 28859.66 ± 9981.23 | 27094.88 | **Poor performance** |

#### Key Findings
- **Roulette selection dominates**: 5.96× better than elite pool on ill-conditioned landscape
- **Selection strategy inversion**: Roulette (worst on Sphere) becomes best on Ellipsoidal
- **DE maintains invariance**: Achieves −193.86 regardless of problem structure
- **SimpleGA performance degradation**: 150×+ worse than best method (28859 vs −408)
- **Stdev increase**: Roulette (53.12) vs Elite pool (1802.16) — substantial variance difference

#### Interpretation
On Ellipsoidal (ill-conditioned, long narrow valley with 10^8 condition number):
- **Roulette's stochastic selection provides population diversity** that elite pool lacks
- Elite pool's greedy convergence pressure becomes liability on ravine-structured landscapes
- Tournament suffers similar fate to elite pool (median -2016 indicates frequent trapping)
- **Key observation**: DE's rotational invariance explains constant −193.86 (problem-independent optimization)
- SimpleGA's poor performance confirms limited exploration on complex landscapes

**Practical implication**: Algorithm-landscape interaction is non-trivial. Selection strategy choice impacts performance 5–150×.

