### 2.5 Rosenbrock Function (Dimension 10)
**Location**: `results/thesis/convergence_rosenbrock_dim10/`

#### Summary Table
| Pipeline | Best Fitness (Mean ± StdDev) | Median | Convergence Behavior |
|----------|---|---|---|
| evosax_differential_evolution | -193.66 ± 0.87 | -193.86 | **BEST** — handles valley |
| malthusjax_tournament | -188.44 ± 0.62 | -188.35 | **BEST MalthusJAX** — tournament wins |
| malthusjax_default | -188.30 ± 0.37 | -188.30 | Elite pool close second |
| malthusjax_roulette | -187.93 ± 0.36 | -187.95 | Slightly weaker on smooth regions |
| evosax_simplega | 141.42 ± 98.67 | 147.53 | **SEVERE FAILURE** — wrong basin |

#### Key Findings
- **DE dominates** (−193.66 vs MalthusJAX −188.44): 5.2 fitness unit gap
- **Tournament outperforms elite pool among MalthusJAX**: First time selection strategy matters for MalthusJAX
- **Tighter clustering than Ellipsoidal**: MalthusJAX variants within 0.5 units (stdev < 0.7 for all)
- **SimpleGA in wrong basin**: Positive fitness (141.42) indicates fundamentally failed search
- **Rosenbrock difficulty**: Even best algorithms only reach −193.66, far from optimum (~−100+ on this scaled version)

#### Interpretation
On Rosenbrock (long, winding valley with parabolic structure):
- **Valley navigation challenge**: Rosenbrock's famous "curved valley" topology
- **Tournament advantage**: Likely due to deterministic determinism maintaining direction through curved valley
- **DE's superior performance**: Differential evolution's mutation strategy naturally adapted for valley-following
- **Roulette regression**: Probabilistic selection less effective when directional pressure needed
- **SimpleGA failure**: Population diversity maintenance insufficient to find valley entrance

**Hypothesis**: Rosenbrock combines Sphere-like (smooth convergence needed) with Ellipsoidal-like (directional pressure needed) requirements. Algorithms balancing both (DE, tournament) excel.

