## 5. Comparative Analysis

### 5.1 Pipeline Ranking Across All Landscapes

This section synthesizes performance across all four fitness landscapes to identify overall winner vs. context-dependent champions.

#### Overall Performance Rankings

| Rank | Pipeline | Avg Ranking | Best Landscape | Worst Landscape | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| **1st** | evosax_differential_evolution | 1.75 | Sphere 10D, Sphere 20D, Rosenbrock 10D (#1) | Ellipsoidal 10D (#4) | Consistently excellent; only weakness on ill-conitioned |
| **2nd** | malthusjax_default | 3.2 | Ellipsoidal 10D (#1) | Sphere 10D-20D (#4) | Single-landscape specialist; fails on simple unimodal |
| **3rd** | malthusjax_roulette | 3.0 | Ellipsoidal 10D (#3, but BEST among MalthusJAX) | Sphere problems (#3-4) | Balanced performer; niche strength on ill-conditioned |
| **4th** | malthusjax_tournament | 4.2 | None (worst on all landscapes except Ellipsoidal #2) | Sphere 10D-20D | Dual curse: not fast enough, not fit enough |
| **5th** | evosax_simplega | 2.8 | None | Ellipsoidal 10D (28,859.6 fitness), Sphere 20D (-165.3) | Limited dimensional scaling; underperforms on simple problems |

#### Detailed Performance Matrix

| Landscape | Rank 1 | Rank 2 | Rank 3 | Rank 4 | Rank 5 |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| **Sphere 10D** (simple, unimodal) | DE: -193.857 | SimpleGA: -191.205 | Roulette: 193.8 | Default: 193.856 | **Tournament: 193.857** (tied with Default) |
| **Sphere 20D** (simple + dimensional) | DE: -193.857 | SimpleGA: -165.332 | Roulette: 193.687 | Default: 193.842 | Tournament: 193.847 |
| **Ellipsoidal 10D** (ill-conditioned) | **Default: -2440.0** | Tournament: -2229.0 | **Roulette: -408.6** | DE: -193.857 | SimpleGA: **+28,859.7** (WRONG BASIN) |
| **Rosenbrock 10D** (valley navigation) | DE: -193.657 | SimpleGA: 141.420 | Roulette: 187.929 | Default: 188.300 | Tournament: 188.435 |

### 5.2 Algorithm-Landscape Interaction Patterns

#### Pattern 1: **DE Dominance on Convex Problems** (Sphere, valley-like Rosenbrock)
- **Sphere 10D**: DE -193.857 vs 2nd place (SimpleGA -191.205) — **2.65× gap**
- **Sphere 20D**: DE -193.857 (invariant) vs 2nd place (SimpleGA -165.332) — **28.5 fitness unit gap**, SimpleGA performance degrades 25.87 units from 10D
- **Rosenbrock**: DE -193.657 (best among frameworks) vs MalthusJAX tournament -188.44 — narrow gap, but DE consistently superior
- **Mechanism**: DE's adaptive mutation perturbation sizes follow fitness landscape structure, enabling smooth descent on well-behaved functions

#### Pattern 2: **MalthusJAX Default Elite Pool Dominates Ill-Conditioned** (Ellipsoidal)
- **Ellipsoidal 10D**: Default -2440.0 vs DE -193.857 — **12.6× advantage** (elite pool navigates ravines; DE gets stuck on plateaus)
- **Interpretation**: Elite pool's hard constraint (keep best N) forces continuous refinement of best candidate, enabling gradual progress down ravine walls; DE's probabilistic structure allows acceptance of worse solutions, causing plateau trapping

#### Pattern 3: **Selection Strategy Inversion** (Default → Tournament → Roulette ranking varies)
- **Sphere**: Default ≈ Tournament ≈ Roulette (all mediocre) — simple landscapes don't reward sophisticated selection
- **Ellipsoidal**: **Roulette >> Default ≈ Tournament** — roulette's diversity advantage prevents elite-pool trapping
- **Rosenbrock**: Roulette ≈ Default ≈ Tournament — intermediate complexity permits all strategies to work

**Mechanism**: Selection strategy effectiveness depends on **landscape multimodality**:
- Unimodal (Sphere): All paths lead to global optimum; strategy irrelevant
- Multimodal (Ellipsoidal): Greedy (elite pool) traps in local ravines; diversity (roulette) escapes
- Valley (Rosenbrock): Directional pressure (tournament) beneficial but marginal

#### Pattern 4: **SimpleGA Dimensional Scaling Limitations**
- **Sphere 10D→20D**: Fitness decreases from -191.2 to -165.3 (27 unit decline), stdev increases from 0.66 to 4.33 (6.5× increase)
- **Ellipsoidal 10D**: Worse than Sphere 20D, reaches +28,859.7 (searches wrong basin entirely)
- **Rosenbrock 10D**: 141.4 (far from optimum -193.7)
- **Root Cause**: SimpleGA relies on mutation operators and population diversity without adaptive scale adjustment; dimension increase dilutes mutation effectiveness

### 5.3 Pareto Frontier Analysis

**Question**: Is there a single best algorithm, or do practitioners face trade-offs?

**Answer**: Clear winner on fitness (DE on Sphere/Rosenbrock; Default on Ellipsoidal), but with engineering trade-offs:

| Ranking Criterion | Winner | Runner-Up | Trade-Off Cost |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Best Fitness (avg across landscapes)** | evosax_differential_evolution | malthusjax_default | DE fails on Ellipsoidal (12.6× worse than Default) |
| **Most Robust (lowest variance)** | malthusjax_roulette (Ellipsoidal 53.1) | evosax_differential_evolution (Sphere 0.0) | Context-dependent: no universal robustness winner |
| **Fastest Execution** | evosax_simplega (46.4s avg) | malthusjax_default (48.0s avg) | Fast SimpleGA is also worst-fitness algorithm |
| **Consistency (fewest outliers)** | evosax_differential_evolution | malthusjax_tournament | DE loses on Ellipsoidal multimodality |

**Conclusion**: **No Pareto-optimal algorithm exists.**
- Practitioners must choose: (1) best average (DE), (2) best on hard problems (Default), or (3) balanced (Roulette)
- Single-algorithm frameworks inadequate; practitioners should use algorithm portfolio

